# Talking-avatar router — route first, render second

## The contract

1. **Preflight first, with the tool — never send a bad asset to a
   render.** Zero-dependency, Python stdlib only:

   ```bash
   python3 scripts/avatar_route.py --image face.png --audio voice.wav \
       --budget free --quality good --vram-gb 2 --gpu-vendor nvidia --lang de
   ```

   Exit codes: `0` = route decided · `1` = preflight errors, no route
   (fix the asset, do not render) · `2` = usage error. See SKILL.md
   for the full contract, `references/backends.md` for the backend
   matrix, `references/tts.md` for voice wiring, `references/pitfalls.md`
   for the 20 known failures.

## Decision table

| Situation | Route |
|---|---|
| budget=free, NVIDIA ≥4GB VRAM | `sadtalker-local` (512px) |
| budget=free, NVIDIA 2GB (e.g. GeForce 930MX class) | `sadtalker-local` 256px, very slow — price cloud GPU as the alternative |
| budget=free, no/weak GPU | no free route — say so, offer `sadtalker-cloud-gpu` (cents-per-clip class) |
| quality=studio, budget allows | `heygen-api`, then `hedra-api` |
| stylized/cartoon/non-human face | API route only — SadTalker needs photographic human faces |
| quick draft | cheapest feasible route, 256px |

## Voice rule

German script → German TTS voice (Piper `thorsten` local, or Edge-TTS
de-DE). Persian script → Persian voice. Never cross voices across
languages. Synthesize to WAV, then re-run preflight on the WAV.

## Limits — say them

The tool routes and preflights; it does not render and does not call
APIs. Cost tiers are indicative (Oct 2026) — re-verify the live
pricing page before spending. Never report "rendered" from a
preflight: exit 0 means "route decided", not "video exists".
